    "body": "## Summary\n\nADR-036 Commit 1: CSS `clear` property support. Six tests. **Zero visible delta** (verified by byte-identical PNG comparison).\n\n## Scope\n\n| Pattern | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| `clear:right` on a float | Jump below prior `float:right` |\n| `clear:left` on a float | Jump below prior `float:left` |\n| `clear:both` on a float | Jump below prior same-side float |\n| `clear:none` | No-op |\n| `clear:*` on a non-float block | Same jump below active float |\n\nImplementation reads `clear` from ComputedStyle in `layout_block_children`, checks `float_bottom > cursor_y` before advancing, and clears `float_right_w`/`float_left_w` after jumping so following narrow-blocks aren't pinned to a float they've cleared past.\n\n## Zero visible delta, honestly verified\n\nByte-identical PNG comparison (clear path vs no-clear path, same source, same viewport 1774):\n\n```\n✓ IDENTICAL\n```\n\nLayout height unchanged at 62295. Current HTML article has no consecutive same-side thumbnails, so no overlap manifests.\n\n**Value is defensive**: the moment any article has two consecutive `float:right` (or `float:left`) figures, without `clear` support they overlap at the right/left edge instead of stacking. `clear` is the CSS-native fix. Also unlocks heading-with-`clear:both` patterns (common in Wikipedia sections that should start below a floated image).\n\n## What this commit does NOT fix\n\n**Nav-like content at x=324 in first viewport** — every screenshot since ADR-029 shows overlap with the article intro.\n\nDiagnostic in this branch confirmed it is **not**:\n- `.navbox` (real navbox lives at y=34880+, way below fold)\n- `.sidebar` (not found in tree — hidden or absent)\n- `.nomobile` (only `.shortdescription.nomobile` at y=233, 23px tall, not the overlap)\n\n**The element is unidentified.** Deferred to a separate diagnostic cycle. The `navbox2` search walked class/id substrings for `navbox|sidebar|nomobile` and found only descendants of the real navbox at y=34880.\n\n## Attribute selectors and floats: already worked\n\nADR-036's original spec (#187) hypothesized both were missing. Measurement refuted:\n- **Attribute selectors**: fully implemented in ADR-008, tested 10/10 forms matching including the exact Wikipedia rule `figure[typeof~='mw:File/Thumb']`\n- **Floats**: already correct per ADR-031, thumbnails position at correct edges\n\nAmendment #188 records the correction. **This commit ships only the honestly-measured residual scope** (`clear`).\n\n## Fifth misdiagnosis in the arc\n\nThe correction record:\n1. ADR-028 — grid was correct, header was the bug\n2. ADR-031 — float \"overlap\" was intro text misread\n3. ADR-034 — SVG intrinsic was 1×1, not 220×35\n4. ADR-035 — \"partial\" finding was correct behavior\n5. **ADR-036 — whole spec premise was a misreading cascade**\n\nEach preserved in place with original spec above, correction below.\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before: 425 cases / 1741 assertions\n- After: **431 cases / 1765 assertions** (+6 / +24)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `clear:right` on float jumps below prior right-float | ✅ |\n| `clear:right` on float:left doesn't jump | ✅ |\n| `clear:both` on float jumps below prior | ✅ |\n| `clear:both` on non-float jumps below | ✅ |\n| No-clear floats overlap (baseline unchanged) | ✅ |\n| No-clear non-float narrows beside (baseline unchanged) | ✅ |\n| **Byte-identical PNG (zero visible delta)** | ✅ |\n| Full suite green | ✅ |\n| CI green | (will be verified post-merge) |\n\n## What's next (deferred)\n\n**Nav overlap diagnostic** — separate ADR. Needs to identify the exact element at x=324 y<900 that overlaps the intro. Diagnostic approach: dump every Box at x<500, y<900 sorted by y, identify the one that isn't a maintenance banner / article paragraph.\n\nRefs #187 #188\n",
